      "evidence": "The page says the pullback k[t^2,t^3] → k[t] 'is bijective but not an isomorphism'. Its image omits t: ex-normalization-cusp, step 6.1, explicitly proves that its monomial exponents belong to {0,2,3,4,...}. Thus this pullback is not surjective. The normalization morphism is bijective on classical points, as step 5.1 proves.",
