      "evidence": "The page asserts that the fibre has 'the two points t=±1' and the node is not unibranch, without excluding characteristic two. The Statement of ex-normalization-node assumes 'characteristic not two', and step 6.1 uses this to distinguish the parameters. In characteristic two, t^2−1=(t−1)^2, so the displayed parametrization has just one classical preimage of the origin; the two-point and non-unibranch conclusions fail.",
